# CODEOWNERS - PROTECTED file.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.
#
# The project's whole verification story rests on one rule: the party that writes the
# code must never control the proof. An agent told to make tests pass takes the cheapest
# path, and the cheapest path in a Rust repository is to edit the test, the lint table,
# the expected count or the CI file. Those are all in this repository, and all of them
# would be the same person.
#
# So every path that can make a green result less meaningful is listed below, and a
# change to any of them requires review from the owner rather than from whoever
# authored the code being proved. Enforce this with branch protection: an approval from
# the owner on these paths, plus the CI gate running from the base branch rather than
# from the pull request branch.
#
# CODEOWNERS cannot address a section of a file, only a whole file. The lint table
# lives inside the root Cargo.toml, so that file is owned whole.
#
# Owner placeholder: the repository owner.

# Gate tests, written by the test-author role from the specs alone.
/tests/                 @KajeJeka

# The FO1_DATA harness and the test author's independent reference decoders.
/crates/fo1-tests/      @KajeJeka

# The specifications, written by the spec-author role.
/docs/spec/             @KajeJeka

# The constants ledger.
/spec/                  @KajeJeka

# Gate tooling: the hygiene, layering, trace and gate scripts.
/tools/                 @KajeJeka

# CI and repository governance, including this file and these templates.
/.github/               @KajeJeka

# The lint relaxations that apply inside tests only.
/clippy.toml            @KajeJeka

# The dependency policy.
/deny.toml              @KajeJeka

# The gate count floors. These can only rise, and only with the owner's approval.
/expected_counts.toml   @KajeJeka

# Approved surviving mutants. A survivor not listed here fails the milestone.
/mutants-allow.md       @KajeJeka

# The workspace lint table: unsafe_code, missing_docs, the unwrap/expect/panic and
# indexing denials, the cast denials, and allow_attributes_without_reason. Most of the
# project's "total reader" and "explicit arithmetic" guarantees are enforced from here.
/Cargo.toml             @KajeJeka